---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { isEnabled } from '../flags';
import '../styles/document-page.css';

const showSidebar = isEnabled('aboutSidebar');
const showProgram = isEnabled('aboutProgram');
const showAdvice = isEnabled('aboutAdvice');
const showCommunity = isEnabled('aboutCommunity');
const showBrand = isEnabled('aboutBrand');
const showHiring = isEnabled('aboutHiring');
---

<Layout title="About | Y Combinator">
  <script>
    import * as userplane from '@workspace/sdk';
    import { getAboutPageFlagsMetadata } from '../flags/utils';

    userplane.set('aboutFlags', getAboutPageFlagsMetadata());

    console.log('setting aboutFlags', getAboutPageFlagsMetadata());
  </script>
  <Header />
  <main class="document-page">
    <div class={`document-container ${!showSidebar ? 'no-sidebar' : ''}`}>
      <!-- Main Content -->
      <article class="document-content">
        <header class="document-header">
          <h1>What Happens at YC</h1>
        </header>

        <div class="document-divider"></div>

        <!-- Introduction -->
        <section class="document-section" id="introduction">
          <h2 class="section-heading">Introduction</h2>
          <p>
            People often ask us what happens at Y Combinator. Here is an overview of what happens
            during the YC program and the benefits you get as a YC founder. You can read more about
            why you should apply to YC <a href="https://www.ycombinator.com/apply">here</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- The YC Program -->
        {
          showProgram && (
            <section class="document-section" id="program">
              <h2 class="section-heading">The YC Program</h2>
              <p>
                YC is a three month program. We now run YC four times a year, in the winter, spring,
                summer, and fall. Here's what happens during the three months of YC:
              </p>

              <h3 id="goal">The Goal</h3>
              <p>
                The overall goal of YC is to help startups really take off. They arrive at YC at all
                different stages. Some haven't even started working yet, and others have been at it
                for more than a year. But whatever stage a startup is at when they arrive, our goal
                is to help them reach a stage where they're ready for the next big leap.
              </p>

              <h3 id="funding">Funding</h3>
              <p>
                YC invests $500,000 in every company on standard terms. Our $500K investment is made
                on 2 separate instruments:
              </p>
              <ul class="document-links">
                <li>
                  We invest $125,000 on a post-money <a href="/safe">safe</a> in return for 7% of
                  your company.
                </li>
                <li>
                  We invest $375,000 on an uncapped <a href="/safe">safe</a> with a Most Favored
                  Nation ("MFN") provision.
                </li>
              </ul>

              <h3 id="groups">Groups</h3>
              <p>
                Every company is assigned to a group. Each group consists of 20-30 companies and is
                led by one or more YC Group Partners. They meet weekly to track progress and provide
                guidance.
              </p>

              <h3 id="office-hours">Office Hours</h3>
              <p>
                Throughout the batch, founders have access to office hours with YC partners. These
                one-on-one sessions help founders work through specific challenges, from product
                development to fundraising strategy.
              </p>

              <h3 id="bookface">Bookface</h3>
              <p>
                Bookface is our internal platform where YC founders can connect with each other and
                with the broader YC community. It's a powerful resource for finding customers,
                recruiting talent, and getting advice from founders who've faced similar challenges.
              </p>

              <h3 id="batch-kickoff">Batch Kickoff</h3>
              <p>
                Each batch begins with an in-person kickoff where founders meet their group
                partners, other founders in their batch, and get oriented to the YC program.
              </p>

              <h3 id="alumni-talks">Alumni Talks</h3>
              <p>
                During the batch, successful YC alumni come to speak with the current batch. These
                talks cover everything from technical challenges to company building to personal
                experiences as a founder.
              </p>

              <h3 id="public-launches">Public Launches</h3>
              <p>
                Once a startup has something built that's ready to launch, we help founders figure
                out how to present it to users and the press. We prepare founders for launches on
                community sites like Product Hunt and Hacker News, and for their first press pitches
                and interviews.
              </p>

              <h3 id="first-customers">First Customers</h3>
              <p>
                B2B and consumer companies often get their first 40-50 paying customers from the YC
                community. With that, you not only get first customers, you get the smartest early
                product feedback possible.
              </p>

              <h3 id="weekly-meetups">Weekly Meetups</h3>
              <p>
                Throughout the batch, we host weekly meetups in San Francisco. These events often
                feature special guests like the founders of YC and successful YC founders.
              </p>

              <h3 id="demo-day">Demo Day</h3>
              <p>
                On <a href="https://www.ycombinator.com/demoday">Demo Day</a>, the latest batch of Y
                Combinator-funded founders present their companies to an audience of specially
                selected investors and press. We doubt there's another occasion when such a large
                percentage of the top startup investors have their attention focused on the same
                thing.
              </p>
              <p>
                In the weeks following Demo Day we keep in close touch with the startups as they
                negotiate the fundraising maze, and help them decipher the real meaning of the
                sometimes ambiguous things investors tell them.
              </p>
            </section>
          )
        }

        <!-- Advice -->
        {
          showAdvice && (
            <section class="document-section" id="advice">
              <h2 class="section-heading">Advice</h2>

              <h3 id="ongoing-office-hours">Ongoing office hours</h3>
              <p>
                After Demo Day, our advice doesn't stop. We continue to help founders with office
                hours as their companies grow. Many YC companies come back to us when they're
                raising Series A, B, or later rounds.
              </p>
            </section>
          )
        }

        <!-- Community -->
        {
          showCommunity && (
            <section class="document-section" id="community">
              <h2 class="section-heading">Community</h2>

              <h3 id="alumni-community">Alumni community</h3>
              <p>
                YC alumni have access to a network of over 10,000 founders who've been through the
                program. This network is invaluable for introductions, advice, and support
                throughout your company's journey.
              </p>

              <h3 id="alumni-reunion">Alumni Reunion</h3>
              <p>
                Once a year, we host an alumni reunion where founders from all batches come together
                to reconnect and learn from each other.
              </p>

              <h3 id="founder-communities">Founder Communities</h3>
              <p>
                YC hosts various communities for founders, including WhatsApp groups organized by
                location, industry, and interests. These communities help founders find peer support
                and share resources.
              </p>

              <h3 id="alumni-demo-day">Alumni Demo Day</h3>
              <p>
                YC alumni get to attend Demo Day and see the newest batch of companies present. Many
                alumni become investors in or advisors to newer YC companies.
              </p>

              <h3 id="deals">Deals</h3>
              <p>
                YC founders get access to over $1M worth of deals from leading software providers.
                These include AWS, Google Cloud, Stripe, and many others.
              </p>
            </section>
          )
        }

        <!-- Brand -->
        {
          showBrand && (
            <section class="document-section" id="brand">
              <h2 class="section-heading">Brand</h2>

              <h3 id="credibility">Credibility</h3>
              <p>
                Being a YC company is a signal to investors, customers, and potential employees that
                you've been vetted by a team with a strong track record of identifying successful
                startups.
              </p>

              <h3 id="company-directory">Company Directory</h3>
              <p>
                Every YC company is listed in our <a href="/">Company Directory</a>, which is
                visited by millions of people each year looking for promising startups to work with
                or invest in.
              </p>
            </section>
          )
        }

        <!-- Hiring -->
        {
          showHiring && (
            <section class="document-section" id="hiring">
              <h2 class="section-heading">Hiring</h2>

              <h3 id="work-at-startup">Work at a Startup</h3>
              <p>
                <a href="https://www.ycombinator.com/jobs">Work at a Startup</a> helps YC founders
                build their team — from first employees to VPs of product and operations. Thousands
                of jobseekers across hundreds of YC companies have landed roles through the platform
                and extended YC community.
              </p>

              <h3 id="hacker-news">Hacker News</h3>
              <p>
                <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/">HN</a> is a news aggregator where users can
                find and discuss the latest news and submit content on anything that gratifies one's
                intellectual curiosity. YC alumni also post engineering, product, and design jobs on
                HN.
              </p>
            </section>
          )
        }
      </article>

      <!-- Sidebar -->
      {
        showSidebar && (
          <aside class="document-sidebar">
            <div class="sidebar-box">
              {showProgram && (
                <>
                  <h4 class="sidebar-title">The YC Program</h4>
                  <ol class="sidebar-nav">
                    <li>
                      <a href="#goal">The Goal</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <a href="#funding">Funding</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <a href="#groups">Groups</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <a href="#office-hours">Office Hours</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <a href="#bookface">Bookface</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <a href="#batch-kickoff">Batch Kickoff</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <a href="#alumni-talks">Alumni Talks</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <a href="#public-launches">Public Launches</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <a href="#first-customers">First Customers</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <a href="#weekly-meetups">Weekly Meetups</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <a href="#demo-day">Demo Day</a>
                    </li>
                  </ol>
                </>
              )}

              {showAdvice && (
                <>
                  <h4 class="sidebar-title">Advice</h4>
                  <ol class="sidebar-nav">
                    <li>
                      <a href="#ongoing-office-hours">Ongoing office hours</a>
                    </li>
                  </ol>
                </>
              )}

              {showCommunity && (
                <>
                  <h4 class="sidebar-title">Community</h4>
                  <ol class="sidebar-nav">
                    <li>
                      <a href="#alumni-community">Alumni community</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <a href="#alumni-reunion">Alumni Reunion</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <a href="#founder-communities">Founder Communities</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <a href="#alumni-demo-day">Alumni Demo Day</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <a href="#deals">Deals</a>
                    </li>
                  </ol>
                </>
              )}

              {showBrand && (
                <>
                  <h4 class="sidebar-title">Brand</h4>
                  <ol class="sidebar-nav">
                    <li>
                      <a href="#credibility">Credibility</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <a href="#company-directory">Company Directory</a>
                    </li>
                  </ol>
                </>
              )}

              {showHiring && (
                <>
                  <h4 class="sidebar-title">Hiring</h4>
                  <ol class="sidebar-nav">
                    <li>
                      <a href="#work-at-startup">Work at a Startup</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <a href="#hacker-news">Hacker News</a>
                    </li>
                  </ol>
                </>
              )}
            </div>
          </aside>
        )
      }
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
